  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Responding to Urgent Needs of Internally Displaced People in Northern and Central Mali</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Mali continues to face a complex, multi-faceted crisis that is driving multi-sectoral humanitarian needs across the country, particularly in the Northern and Central regions where most of the country&apos;s hotbeds of conflict and violence are located.Through this project, IOM aims to respond to the urgent needs resulting from population displacement in central and northern Mali by reducing vulnerabilities and improving the protection and living conditions of displaced populations and host communities. Vulnerable households among the displaced and host communities are going to have access to shelter, non-food items (NFIs) and water, sanitation and hygiene (WASH) assistance, and the capacity to respond, plan and manage displacement sites is being strengthened for better responsiveness in terms of direct emergency assistance.</narrative>
  </description>
